# "At the beginning of each opponent's upkeep" (CR 603.2b): in a three-player game the Oculus manifests dread on Bot2's
# upkeep (turn 2) and on Bot3's (turn 3), and does nothing on its controller's own upkeep (turn 4). Each manifest looks at
# the top two cards, so the library goes down by two each time (the face-down card and the one to the graveyard) and
# (Bot1 draws on turn 1, as the first player of three, so a spare Island is discarded too.) It stays put on turn 4.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Black Lotus
Wheel of Fortune
Island x5
Mox Sapphire
Sol Ring
Abhorrent Oculus
Island x4
Forest x2
Plains x2
Island x6

[Bot2 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Bot3 Deck]
Swamp x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Wheel of Fortune.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Abhorrent Oculus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Island; Island; Island; Island; Black Lotus; Wheel of Fortune)
[T2 Bot2.Upkeep]
? Bot1.Library.Count = 10
Bot1.Arrange(Forest | Forest)
[T3 Bot3.Upkeep]
Bot1.Arrange(Plains | Plains)
[T4 Bot1.Upkeep]
? Bot1.Library.Count = 6
[T4 Bot1.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot1.Library.Count = 5
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 3
Bot1.Battlefield.Count = 6
